  "question": {
    "text": "A tuning fork is vibrating at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The length of the shortest closed organ pipe that will resonate with the tuning fork will be _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>. (Take speed of sound in air as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "34",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For closed organ pipe</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>for minimum length, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>340</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>250</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>",
